<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.8.2: Using the Distributive Property to Write Equivalent Expressions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01868</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.8.2: Using the Distributive Property to Write Equivalent Expressions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b5ab0794-daaf-4146-b8ee-89f6e0728f42</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Applying the distributive property to multiply out the factors of, or
        expand, <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mn>4</m:mn>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            <m:mo>+</m:mo>
            <m:mn>2</m:mn>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math> gives us <m:math
          display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mn>4</m:mn>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            <m:mo>+</m:mo>
            <m:mn>8</m:mn>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math>, so we know the two expressions are
        equivalent. We can use a rectangle with side lengths <m:math display="inline">
          <m:mrow>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
            <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            <m:mo>+</m:mo>
            <m:mn>2</m:mn>
            <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
          </m:mrow>
        </m:math> and 4 to illustrate
        the multiplication.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">
        <media
          alt="Rectangle, divided into 2 smaller rectangles. Top of left rectangle labeled x, top of right rectangle labeled 2. Side length labeled 4. Inside left rectangle, 4 x.">
          <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_10_03_01.svg" />
        </media>

      </para>

      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">Draw a diagram to show that <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> and <m:math
              display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math> are equivalent
            expressions.</para>
          <para id="para-00004">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00005">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00006">
            <media alt="Area model multiplying 2n+5 and n">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_10_03_02.svg" />
            </media>

          </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>


      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">For each expression, use the distributive property to write an
            equivalent expression. If you get stuck, consider drawing a diagram.</para>
          <para id="para-00008"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>6</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00009">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00011"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mi>n</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>12</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>


      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00012"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>9</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00013">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00014">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00015"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>9</m:mn>
                <m:mi>p</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>


      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00016"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                <m:mi>r</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mi>r</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mfrac>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:mfrac>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00017">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00018">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00019"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>r</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                <m:mi>r</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>


      <exercise id="exer-00005">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00020"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>0.5</m:mn>
                <m:mi>w</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mi>w</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00021">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00022">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00023"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>0.5</m:mn>
                <m:msup>
                  <m:mi>w</m:mi>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:msup>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                <m:mi>w</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>

    </section>

    <note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
      <exercise id="exer-00007">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00024"><link class="os-embed" url="#exercise/Alg1_7_8_2_SC" /></para>
        </problem>
      </exercise>
    </note>

    <section>
      <title>Additional Resources</title>
      <section id="sect-00002">
        <title>Distributive Property </title>

        <para id="para-00025">
          <emphasis> Distributive Property</emphasis>
        </para>

        <para id="para-00026">If <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>, <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>, <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>c</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> are real numbers, then:</para>
        <para id="para-00027"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mi>c</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              <m:mi>c</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00028">Other forms:</para>
        <para id="para-00029"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mi>c</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              <m:mi>c</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00030"><m:math>
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mi>c</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mi>b</m:mi>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mi>c</m:mi>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00031">
          <emphasis>Example 1</emphasis>
        </para>
        <para id="para-00032">Simplify <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00033"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Distribute the 3 to both the <m:math
            display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and the 4. <media
            alt="DIAGRAM SHOWING 3 MULTIPLIED BY X PLUS 4. AN ARROW IS GOING FROM 3 TO X. ANOTHER ARROW IS GOING FROM 3 TO 4.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_10_05_01.jpg" />
          </media></para>
        <para id="para-00034"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Multiply the terms.</para><para><m:math
            display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00035"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Simplify.</para><para><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mn>12</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00036">
          <emphasis>Example 2</emphasis>
        </para>
        <para id="para-00037">Simplify <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>7</m:mn>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00038"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Distribute the <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> to both the 7 and the <m:math
            display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>. <media
            alt="DIAGRAM SHOWING M TIMES 7 MINUS 2M. AN ARROW IS GOING FROM M TO 7. ANOTHER ARROW IS GOING FROM M TO 2M.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_10_05_02.jpg" />
          </media></para>
        <para id="para-00039"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Multiply the terms. Recall <m:math
            display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.</para><para><m:math
            display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>7</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00040"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Simplify.</para><para><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>7</m:mn>
              <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>
        </para>
        <para id="para-00041">
          <emphasis>Example 3</emphasis>
        </para>
        <para id="para-00042">Simplify <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00043"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Distribute the <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> to both the <m:math
            display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math> and the <m:math
            display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>. <media
            alt="DIAGRAM SHOWING 5X TIMES X MINUS TWO-FIFTHS. AN ARROW IS GOING FROM 5X TO X. ANOTHER ARROW IS GOING FROM 5X TO TWO-FIFTHS.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_10_05_03.jpg" />
          </media></para>
        <para id="para-00044"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Multiply the terms. Recall <m:math
            display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mi>·</m:mi>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>.</para><para><m:math
            display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00045"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Simplify.</para><para><m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>5</m:mn>
              <m:msup>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:msup>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
        <note class="try" id="note-00002">
          <title>Try It: Distributive Property</title>
      
        <exercise id="exer-00006">
            <problem id="prob-00006">
              <para id="para-00046">Simplify <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00047">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
          button to compare your work.</para>
            </problem>
            <solution id="sol-00006">
              <para id="para-00048">Here is how to simplify the expression using the distributive
          property:</para>
              <para id="para-00049"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Distribute the <m:math
                  display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math> to both the <m:math
                  display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math> and the <m:math
                  display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>
          .</para>
              <para id="para-00050">
                <media
                  alt="DIAGRAM SHOWING 7Y TIMES 4Y MINUS THREE-SEVENTHS. AN ARROW IS GOING FROM 7Y TO 4Y. ANOTHER ARROW IS GOING FROM 7Y TO THREE-SEVENTHS.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_10_05_04.jpg" />
                </media>

              </para>
              <para id="para-00051"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Multiply the terms. Recall <m:math
                  display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                    <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                    <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math>
          .
    <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                    <m:mfrac>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                      <m:mrow>
                        <m:mn>7</m:mn>
                      </m:mrow>
                    </m:mfrac>
                    <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
              <para id="para-00052"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Simplify. <m:math display="inline">
                  <m:mrow>
                    <m:mn>28</m:mn>
                    <m:msup>
                      <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                      <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                    </m:msup>
                    <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                    <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                    <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                  </m:mrow>
                </m:math></para>
            </solution>
          </exercise>
        </note>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>